 patho:"Ischemic strokes (most strokes) come from thrombus or embolus; clot-dissolving therapy may help if given within a narrow time window and bleeding is ruled out by CT. Hemorrhagic strokes come from a ruptured vessel; anticoagulants are dangerous. Deficits appear on the side of the body opposite the brain injury.",
