 patho:"Portal hypertension causes varices and ascites. Low albumin lowers oncotic pressure (edema, ascites). Ammonia from gut protein isn't converted to urea, causing encephalopathy. Reduced clotting factors raise bleeding risk.",
 risk:["Chronic alcohol use, hepatitis B or C, fatty liver disease"],
 findings:["Jaundice, ascites, spider angiomas, easy bruising","Encephalopathy: confusion → asterixis (flapping tremor) → stupor → coma; fetor hepaticus"],
 red:["Vomiting blood (ruptured varices): airway and circulation emergency","Worsening orientation or asterixis","Hypovolemia after large-volume paracentesis"],
 assess:["Orientation and asterixis","Abdominal girth and daily weight","Bleeding: stools, gums, PT/INR, platelets","Ammonia, albumin, bilirubin"],
 prio:["Airway and bleeding first with varices","Safety and neuro status with encephalopathy","Avoid hepatotoxic and sedating drugs"],
